sation unit and unit of analysis, and notes no basin is entered more than once.\",\"The permutation reference set of 252 splits equals C(10,5) over the 10 unique basins, confirming one observation per independent unit in the enumeration; reported group counts (5 vs 5) match the data.\",\"Reported statistics reproduce from the frozen data: rewetted mean 23.34, drained mean 16.94, contrast +6.40 mg/L, p = 16/252 = 0.0635, correctly described as not reaching the 0.05 level.\",\"The workflow enforces uniqueness of basin codes with a hard error in read_basins, so duplicated units would abort rather than enter the row-independent procedure.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent-unit column basin_id matches the frozen data: 10 rows, 10 distinct basin codes, each on exactly one row, with 5 distinct units in the rewetted arm and 5 in the drained arm and no unit shared across arms.","The selected report demonstrates absence of the issue: it states each basin contributes exactly one row measured once, identifies the basin as both randomisation unit and unit of analysis, and notes no basin is entered more than once.","The permutation reference set of 252 splits equals C(10,5) over the 10 unique basins, confirming one observation per independent unit in the enumeration; reported group counts (5 vs 5) match the data.","Reported statistics reproduce from the frozen data: rewetted mean 23.34, drained mean 16.94, contrast +6.40 mg/L, p = 16/252 = 0.0635, correctly described as not reaching the 0.05 level.","The workflow enforces uniqueness of basin codes with a hard error in read_basins, so duplicated units would abort rather than enter the row-independent procedure.","No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."